  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PSE 1 - Regional responses to criminal justice systems responses to the threat of maritime crime</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching objective of this PSED is to &quot;strengthen the capabilities of the entire criminal justice chain in the Gulf of Guinea to respond to the threat of maritime crime&quot;. 

Thus, the intervention includes efforts aimed at enhancing the capabilities of state actors to detect, interdict, investigate and prosecute maritime crimes, as well as to detain maritime criminals in accordance with international human rights law, with a focus also on regional cooperation. Furthermore, the PSED also seeks to promote the Women, Peace and Security agenda in the region, as applicable to maritime security and maritime law enforcement. 

The PSED will focus on Gulf of Guinea maritime security institutions and countries, particularly those within Zones E, F and D, including Benin, Cameroun, C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, Ghana, Nigeria and Togo.</narrative>
  </description>
